<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>O who like Thee, so mild, so bright,</l><l>Thou Son of man, Thou Light of light?</l><l>O who like Thee did ever go</l><l>So patient, through a world of woe?</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>O who like Thee so humbly bore</l><l>The scorn, the scoffs of men, before?</l><l>So meek, so lowly, yet so high,</l><l>So glorious in humility?</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>And death, that sets the prisoner free,</l><l>Was pang, and scoff, and scorn to Thee;</l><l>Yet love through all Thy torture glowed,</l><l>And mercy with Thy life-blood flowed.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>O wondrous Lord, my soul would be</l><l>Still more and more conformed to Thee,</l><l>And learn of Thee, the lowly One,</l><l>And like Thee, all my journey run.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
